<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Eastman Kodak to create 360 more jobs in Cork.</title>
<headline>Eastman Kodak to create 360 more jobs in Cork.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's Minister for Enterprise and Employment Richard Bruton said on Monday that Eastman Kodak has agreed a further 39 million punt investment proposal with Irish industrial development agency IDA Ireland.</p>
<p>This will create 360 new jobs in addition to the 250 jobs announced less than a year ago at the Kodak Cork Ltd plant in Youghal in southern Ireland, Bruton said in a statement.</p>
<p>Kodak Cork Ltd was set up by the U.S.-based company last year to manufacture recordable compact discs for the European market.</p>
<p>--Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9775</p>
</text>
